{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794532166302,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e351cffeKi2fx1OYLz9itX","part":{"partID":"prt_1d273c808002qzEvm47uYYE0sc","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e351cffeKi2fx1OYLz9itX","messageID":"msg_1d273c208001XNEeXT5R0XAZDD","type":"tool","id":"call_ca1214ff4b934760a2fb6749","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs","offset":160,"limit":35},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs, lines 160-194\n160:   `B) ${GATE_3_CHOICE_NEW} (reply with a new path, e.g. specs/<track>/<NNN-name>)`,\n161:   'C) Use a related spec folder or phase child, or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact as an existing packet in the same track (reply with its path, e.g. specs/<track>/<NNN-name> or specs/<parent>/<NNN-phase>)',\n162:   'D) Skip (no spec folder needed for this change)',\n163: ].join('\\n');\n164: \n165: // The model-facing mutation-time notice. Deliberately NOT a bare question: a\n166: // question dropped into a turn reads as a blocking instruction to an\n167: // instruction-literal model, which then stops on every write-intent turn. This\n168: // states the once-per-session contract in the text itself as well, so a runtime\n169: // that cannot remember a delivery still stops asking after the first answer.\n170: export const GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE = [\n171:   'SPEC FOLDER QUESTION - this session has no bound spec folder and a file mutation is about to run.',\n172:   'Ask the operator once where this change should live. Recommend one option first and say why, never a neutral menu. Then continue:',\n173:   `A) ${GATE_3_CHOICE_EXISTING} - reply with its path, e.g. specs/<track>/<NNN-name>`,\n174:   `B) ${GATE_3_CHOICE_NEW} - reply with its path, e.g. specs/<track>/<NNN-name> (it does not have to exist yet)`,\n175:   'C) A related folder, a phase child, or a series parent for a different change to the same artifact as an existing packet in the same track - reply with its path',\n176:   `D) ${GATE_3_CHOICE_SKIP}`,\n177:   'The answer holds for the rest of this session: do not ask this again on later turns.',\n178:   'For a new folder, start /speckit:plan, or /speckit:complete when the operator asked for the build itself: read that command document in full and follow it without :auto.',\n179:   'Once the folder is chosen, write its spec documents by following .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/spec-authoring-card.md.',\n180: ].join('\\n');\n181: \n182: // Where no dialog exists to ask at the mutation, the classify surface still has\n183: // to tell the model what the open gate means without stopping the turn it is on\n184: // -- a deferral, not a question, so it cannot be read as a blocking request.\n185: export const GATE_3_DEFERRED_INSTRUCTION = [\n186:   'SPEC GATE: this session needs a spec-folder decision, but only at the first file mutation.',\n187:   'Do not stop to ask it now; ask it once when you are about to write, then continue.',\n188: ].join('\\n');\n189: \n190: // The human-facing relay question above and the model-facing deny reason\n191: // below are deliberately different strings: GATE_3_QUESTION is what the USER\n192: // sees (a menu to answer); GATE_3_DENY_DETAIL is what the MODEL sees when a\n193: // Write/Edit is actually blocked -- an instruction to go get that answer from\n194: // the user, not a menu the model itself could try to resolve alone. The\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 195]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs, lines 160-194\n160:   `B) ${