{"type":"text","timestamp":1794532213121,"sessionID":"ses_e2d8e351cffeKi2fx1OYLz9itX","part":{"id":"prt_1d27476000028ubySZmYvGPGxr","sessionID":"ses_e2d8e351cffeKi2fx1OYLz9itX","messageID":"msg_1d2746dc4001juL6VHYASM1WBy","type":"text","text":"**T020 complete.**\n\n## Files written\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tests/hooks/spec-gate-core.test.mjs` — added the T012 line to the `mutationNotice` array in the test `Gate-3 delivery flag off preserves byte-identical baseline output`, immediately after `'The answer holds for the rest of this session: ...'`, matching its position in `GATE_3_MUTATION_NOTICE`.\n\nDiff is exactly one added line. No other file touched.\n\n## Verify output\nCommand as written in the task, run from `$SSK` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime`):\n\n```\nℹ tests 110\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 107\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 3\nℹ todo 0\n```\n\n`fail 0` and `pass 107` as expected. The edited test passed.\n\n## Caveat worth recording\nThis dispatched worker runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` and `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=0` set. Run verbatim under that inherited environment, the same file reported `pass 57 / fail 50`, because those variables force the spec gate closed and ~50 unrelated gate-state tests assert `'open'`. The edited test itself passed in that run too. Re-running with `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD -u SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE` produces the clean `pass 107 / fail 0` above. Any later verification of T030 should run without the dispatch exemption variables.\n\nI did not tick the T020 checkbox in `tasks.md`, per instructions.","time":{"start":1794532210176,"end":1794532213121}}}
